# TUI-DESIGN-4 §7.3 item 4: in the boxed tier the status line is a `status={…}` PROP of <Console>, inside the
# composer's boundary — so a StatusLine throw used to take the whole console box with it for the rest of the run
# (measured). With the status wrapped in its own boundary ONE ROW degrades and the four box characters survive.
# JEVCODE_FAULT=render:status.
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 0.8
send hi
sleep 0.2
send \r
sleep 0.8
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
